Package: CPTACdata
Title: Append CPTAC Proteomics Data to MultiAssayExperiment Objects
Version: 0.99.9
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marcel", "Ramos", , "marcel.ramos@sph.cuny.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3242-0582")),
    person("Claude", "Haiku 5.5", , "noreply@anthropic.com",
           role = "ctb"))
Description: Integrates proteomic data from the Clinical Proteomic
    Tumor Analysis Consortium (CPTAC) into existing MultiAssayExperiment
    objects containing The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) patient barcodes.
    The package queries the Proteomic Data Commons (PDC) GraphQL API
    to resolve studies by disease type and fetch quantitative protein
    log2 ratio matrices and biospecimen identifiers.
    It harmonizes TCGA barcodes with CPTAC case identifiers, constructs
    SummarizedExperiment objects whose colData holds the matched biospecimen
    identifiers and sample types, and appends the proteomic assays to the
    MultiAssayExperiment. It also downloads the CPTAC-3 and CPTAC-2
    Prospective cohorts, which use their own patients, as
    MultiAssayExperiment objects with one experiment per PDC study and the
    PDC clinical data as colData.
